{"family": "depth_pro", "task": "depth", "name": "Depth Pro", "plain": "Apple's single-image model for metric depth and the camera focal length, at 1536x1536 internal resolution. Research-only licence.", "summary": "Depth Pro (Bochkovskii et al. 2024, Apple): sharp monocular metric depth from three DINOv2 ViT-L/16 encoders (35 overlapping windows of a 3-level image pyramid, the whole image, the field of view) and a multi-resolution conv decoder at 1536x1536; also estimates the focal length.", "tier": "stable", "upstream": "https://github.com/apple/ml-depth-pro", "upstream_commit": "9e65e4d", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "Depth Pro: Sharp Monocular Metric Depth in Less Than a Second", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.02073", "date": "2024-10-02", "venue": "ICLR 2025", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fastbb", "dpt_fused"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [], "outputs": [{"name": "depth", "extra": false}, {"name": "intrinsics", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "metric"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": ["The Apple sample-code licence and the model licence allow research use only."], "limitations": [], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant` and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v2-vitl14`, `unik3d-vitl`, `depth-pro` and MoGe estimate the camera them